Version control is essential for managing cloud infrastructure and configuration files. Every infrastructure change should be tracked, reviewed, and documented to improve collaboration and reduce deployment risks.

Advantages include:

* Complete change history
* Easier collaboration
* Rollback capability
* Code reviews
* Improved auditing
* Better documentation

For example, if a networking configuration causes unexpected connectivity issues, administrators can compare previous versions and restore a known working configuration.

A real-life use case is cloud engineering teams collaborating across multiple locations while maintaining a single source of truth for infrastructure definitions.

Version control strengthens governance and operational reliability.
